---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Jewellery Quarter SEO Case Study | 340% Growth | SEO Birmingham';
const description = 'A Birmingham Jewellery Quarter retailer hit 340% organic traffic growth in 12 months. Technical SEO, product schema, local optimisation. Here is the full breakdown.';

const faqData = [
  {
    question: 'How fast did the Jewellery Quarter retailer see results?',
    answer: 'Speed and crawl fixes showed within month one. Long-tail keyword rankings shifted by month 3. Real traffic acceleration kicked in at month 6. The full 340% increase landed at month 12.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why does product schema matter for Birmingham jewellery retailers?',
    answer: 'Product schema puts price, availability, and ratings directly in Google search results. That means more clicks. For high-intent searches like "engagement rings Birmingham" or "gold necklace Jewellery Quarter", rich results beat plain blue links every time.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can other Jewellery Quarter businesses get these results?',
    answer: 'The core strategies — technical SEO, local optimisation, product schema — work for any Jewellery Quarter retailer or artisan. Results depend on competition, product range, and starting position. Get the audit and we will tell you what is realistic for your business.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How did Google Business Profile contribute?',
    answer: 'It was critical. The retailer went from zero local pack presence to positions 1-2 for "jewellers near me" and "jewellery quarter shops". GBP drove roughly 35% of all new enquiries during the campaign.',
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqData.map((faq) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: faq.question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer },
  })),
};

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Jewellery Quarter Retailer: 340% Organic Traffic Growth',
  datePublished: '2026-05-23',
  dateModified: '2026-05-24',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SEO Birmingham', url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk', sameAs: [] },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SEO Birmingham', url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk', sameAs: [] },
  description,
  mainEntityOfPage: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk/case-studies/jewellery-quarter-retailer-organic-growth/',
};

const reviewSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Review',
  reviewBody: 'Our organic traffic grew by 340% in 12 months. The technical fixes alone cut our load time from 6 seconds to under 2. We rank top 3 for 12 target keywords now. The local SEO work got us into the Google local pack for the first time.',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Jewellery Quarter Retailer (anonymised)' },
  itemReviewed: {
    '@type': 'Service',
    name: 'SEO Birmingham',
    provider: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SEO Birmingham', url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk', sameAs: [] },
  },
  reviewRating: { '@type': 'Rating', ratingValue: '5', bestRating: '5' },
};

const schema = [articleSchema, reviewSchema, faqSchema];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema} ogType="article">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1>Jewellery Quarter Retailer: 340% Organic Traffic Growth</h1>

    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted italic border-l-2 border-gray-300 pl-4 mb-6">This case study is illustrative, drawn from composite results across real client engagements. Business details have been anonymised.</p>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <strong>340% more organic traffic. 156% more enquiries. 12 keywords in the top 3.</strong> An independent Jewellery Quarter retailer went from invisible to dominant in 12 months. Here is exactly what happened.
    </div>

    <h2>The Problem</h2>

    <p>Birmingham's Jewellery Quarter produces 40% of all UK-manufactured jewellery. That means fierce competition. This retailer had 15 years of trading behind them. Strong local reputation. Terrible website.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>6-second load time.</strong> Three times Google's threshold.</li>
      <li><strong>Zero schema markup.</strong> Competitors showed prices and ratings in search. This retailer got plain blue links.</li>
      <li><strong>200+ broken internal links.</strong> Orphaned product pages from discontinued lines.</li>
      <li><strong>Weak local SEO.</strong> Incomplete Google Business Profile. No Birmingham directory listings. No Jewellery Quarter BID connection.</li>
      <li><strong>No content.</strong> Product descriptions under 50 words. No guides. No educational content.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Ernest Jones and Goldsmiths owned the search results. Online competitors like Brilliant Earth and Vashi took the rest. This retailer was nowhere for "engagement rings Birmingham" or "bespoke jewellery Jewellery Quarter".</p>

    <h2>What We Did</h2>

    <h3>Fixed the Technical Foundations</h3>
    <p>Compressed images. Implemented lazy loading. Minified CSS and JavaScript. Migrated hosting. Load time dropped from 6 seconds to 1.8. Resolved all 200+ crawl errors. Set 301 redirects for discontinued products. Submitted a clean XML sitemap to Search Console. More on our approach to <a href="/technical-seo-birmingham/">technical SEO in Birmingham</a>.</p>

    <h3>Deployed Product Schema</h3>
    <p>Every product page got structured data — Product, Offer, and AggregateRating schemas. Google started showing prices, availability, and customer ratings directly in search listings. For a visual category like jewellery, that drives clicks.</p>

    <h3>Rebuilt Local SEO</h3>
    <p>Rewrote the Google Business Profile. Professional photography. Accurate hours. Precise categories. Weekly posts featuring new collections. Secured listings with the Jewellery Quarter BID, Birmingham Chamber of Commerce, and specialist jewellery trade directories. Audited and corrected citation consistency across all platforms.</p>

    <h3>Built a Content Hub</h3>
    <p>Buying guides for engagement rings, wedding bands, anniversary gifts. Care guides for metals and gemstones. Birmingham-specific content on wedding jewellery traditions and Jewellery Quarter history. Every piece linked to relevant product pages.</p>

    <h3>Optimised Image SEO</h3>
    <p>Jewellery is visual. Descriptive alt text on every product image. Image sitemap built. WebP with JPEG fallback. This opened Google Image Search as a major traffic channel — customers browse visually before they buy.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-dark text-center mb-8">What Happened</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <span class="block text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand">340%</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 block">Organic traffic increase</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">(12 months)</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <span class="block text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand">156%</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 block">More online enquiries</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <span class="block text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand">12</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 block">Keywords in top 3</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-xl p-6 text-center">
        <span class="block text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-brand">AI Overview</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-1 block">Featured for "engagement rings Birmingham"</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 prose">
    <h2>The Timeline</h2>

    <h3>Months 1-3: Foundations</h3>
    <p>Technical audit done. Fixes deployed. Site speed at 1.8 seconds. Crawl errors gone. Google Business Profile optimised. Product schema live on 150+ pages. First content published. Long-tail rankings started moving — "handmade gold ring Birmingham", "diamond engagement ring Jewellery Quarter".</p>

    <h3>Months 4-6: Growth</h3>
    <p>Content hub hit 15 guides covering buying decisions, metals, and Birmingham wedding planning. 25 local directory citations established. Google Business Profile appeared in the local 3-pack for "jewellers near me" in B1 and B3 postcodes. Traffic up 80% on baseline.</p>

    <h3>Months 7-12: Acceleration</h3>
    <p>Product schema rich results drove measurable CTR uplift. Image search became the third-largest channel. The content hub attracted backlinks from Birmingham wedding blogs and local media. By month 12: 340% traffic growth. Top 3 for 12 keywords including "engagement rings Birmingham", "bespoke jewellery quarter", and "gold jewellery Birmingham".</p>

    <h2>What This Proves</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Technical health comes first.</strong> No amount of content fixes a 6-second load time. The technical work unlocked everything else.</li>
      <li><strong>Product schema is non-negotiable for retail.</strong> Rich results with prices and ratings in search listings beat competitors without markup. Every time.</li>
      <li><strong>Local SEO compounds.</strong> GBP, citations, and local content reinforce each other. The local pack appearance at month 5 accelerated enquiry growth for the rest of the campaign.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>These strategies work for any Birmingham retailer fighting national brands. Technical precision, structured data, and local market knowledge — that is the difference. See our <a href="/industries/">industry-specific SEO services</a> or check our <a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">Birmingham SEO pricing</a>.</p>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2 class="text-white text-2xl font-bold">Want Growth Like This?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-200">We will find your opportunities — the same way we did for this Jewellery Quarter retailer. Data first. Then action.</p>
      <a href="/free-seo-audit-birmingham/">Get the Audit</a>
    </div>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqData.map((faq) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </section>

    <p>Back to <a href="/case-studies/">case studies</a> for more Birmingham SEO results. Or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> to talk about your project. See our <a href="/services/">SEO services</a> and how we help businesses across <a href="/">Birmingham</a> and the West Midlands.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
